3. Dependency licence review
----------------------------

Reviewed 2026-09-29 over the 120 distributions installed by `uv.lock`.

    MIT              fastapi, pydantic, PyJWT, mcp, PyYAML, SQLAlchemy, pytest, …
    Apache-2.0       a2a-sdk, openai, gradio, sentence-transformers, asyncpg, …
    BSD-3-Clause     uvicorn, starlette, httpx, Jinja2, numpy, scikit-learn, …
    MPL-2.0          certifi; orjson and tqdm in part
    PSF-2.0          typing_extensions, pywin32
    dual             cryptography (Apache-2.0 OR BSD-3-Clause), packaging, torch

**No GPL, LGPL or AGPL dependency.** Nothing in the set constrains redistributing
erebots under the MIT licence.

The three MPL-2.0 packages carry file-level copyleft: the obligation attaches to
*their* files and only if those files are modified, which does not happen here.
They impose nothing on MIT-licensed source that merely imports them.

This review is a snapshot, not a guarantee. Re-run it when `uv.lock` changes in a
way that adds a distribution, and record the date above.
